A monotonic stack is not a different data structure. It is a regular stack with an additional rule: maintain increasing or decreasing order.

    Regular Stack	                 Monotonic Stack
new ArrayDeque<>()	            new ArrayDeque<>()
Push directly	                Check before pushing
No ordering restriction	        Maintains increasing/decreasing order
General-purpose	                Useful for next greater/smaller problems